course: dictionary
lesson: 7046
title: Feeling in the word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some adverbs tell you how something is done. Passionately tells you the doing is full of strong feeling. Read the words around it: what is the person doing, and how do they seem to feel? «She spoke passionately about animals.» The word spoke tells you what she did, and passionately tells you she meant every word.
explain: Ask the sentence a question: would the person be calm and quiet about this, or full of feeling? «Lily finds three kids who argue passionately about whether T. rex had feathers.» Arguing is already strong, and passionately shows how much they care about being right.
explain: Try the swap check. Replace passionately with «calmly» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it sounds strange, passionately must mean with strong feeling. Words often found with it are speak passionately, care passionately and believe passionately.
fact: Passionately is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Passionately» means with very strong feeling or enthusiasm.
fact: «Passionately» can also mean very much or deeply, as in «He passionately believes in fairness.»
fact: In stories and songs, passionately can show strong love, anger or belief.
fact: Its other forms are more passionately and most passionately.
exercise: «She spoke passionately about animals.» What does passionately tell us about how she spoke? | Very quietly, almost in a whisper | Without stopping to breathe | While she was half asleep | *With very strong feeling
exercise: «Lily finds three kids who argue passionately about whether T. rex had feathers.» Which word is the adverb? | *passionately | argue | feathers | kids
exercise: Maya wants a new park and talks about it with shining eyes and great energy. Which word fits best? She speaks ___ about the park. | *passionately | lazily | carelessly
test: «He passionately believes in fairness.» What does passionately mean here? | Not at all | Quickly, in a rush | Very slowly | *Very much, deeply
test: Dad says, «I care passionately about our town.» Which sentence means the same? | Dad doesn't care about the town at all | Dad only cares about the town in the morning | *Dad cares very deeply about the town | Dad cares a little, but not much
exam: In a song, the singer sings passionately about lost love. What does passionately suggest here? | Badly and out of tune | Only on Tuesdays | Very quietly, with no feeling | *With strong love and emotion
